          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Single-trigger acceleration vests all unvested options on a change of control event (acquisition, merger, IPO). Double-trigger acceleration requires both a change of control event AND a termination without cause of the employee within a defined window (typically 12 months). Double-trigger is investor-friendly and now the Series B-plus market norm in Delhi."
          }
        },
